From: oneplus6t port <none@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: u_ether: guard NULL skb from ncm_tx_tasklet

eth_start_xmit() can be called with skb == NULL. f_ncm.c does this
deliberately when flushing a partially filled NTB:

    ncm->netdev->netdev_ops->ndo_start_xmit(NULL, ncm->netdev);

Two paths then dereference the NULL skb:

1. The "no IN endpoint" bail-out is written as

       if (skb && !in) { ... return NETDEV_TX_OK; }

   so when the gadget has been torn down (dev->port_usb == NULL, hence
   in == NULL) *and* skb is NULL, it falls through instead of returning.

2. The CDC/RNDIS filter block then runs

       u8 *dest = skb->data;

   unconditionally. With port_usb NULL, cdc_filter is left 0, so
   is_promisc(0) is false and the block is entered.

The result is a NULL dereference at offsetof(struct sk_buff, data) == 0xd0
in softirq context, which is fatal:

    Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 000000d0
    PC is at eth_start_xmit+0x80/0x6c0
    Call trace:
      eth_start_xmit
      ncm_tx_tasklet
      tasklet_action
      __do_softirq
    Kernel panic - not syncing: Fatal exception in interrupt

This reproduces reliably on Droidian: the halium initramfs brings up an
RNDIS gadget, then userspace reconfigures the gadget to NCM over configfs.
The NCM tx tasklet fires against the half-torn-down netdev and panics the
kernel about five seconds after systemd starts. Android never hits it
because it does not use NCM.

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/u_ether.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/u_ether.c
index c75e790d2..1aa21e7e4 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/u_ether.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/u_ether.c
@@ -788,13 +788,14 @@ static netdev_tx_t eth_start_xmit(struct sk_buff *skb,
 	}
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&dev->lock, flags);
 
-	if (skb && !in) {
-		dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
+	if (!in) {
+		if (skb)
+			dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
 		return NETDEV_TX_OK;
 	}
 
 	/* apply outgoing CDC or RNDIS filters */
-	if (!test_bit(RMNET_MODE_LLP_IP, &dev->flags) &&
+	if (skb && !test_bit(RMNET_MODE_LLP_IP, &dev->flags) &&
 			!is_promisc(cdc_filter)) {
 		u8		*dest = skb->data;
 
